  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146682",
      "title": "Using the \"useEffect\" Hook",
      "lectureOrder": 78,
      "videoOrder": 73,
      "sourceHash": "f559cb1d0b529bb9052f721c8a44596079c4cd51a2fb7fd55988d73d3cc8210b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.23,
          "end": 5.41,
          "en": "So how can we work around that problem?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.41,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "This is such a common problem and such a common scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 12.4,
          "en": "that React has a solution for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.4,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "There is another hook which you can import from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 17.653,
          "en": "and that's the useEffect hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 23.17,
          "en": "UseEffect is a hook that allows you to run some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.17,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "under certain conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 28.93,
          "en": "At the moment this code for sending the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.93,
          "end": 32.68,
          "en": "runs always when the component function runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.68,
          "end": 36.73,
          "en": "With useEffect we'll be able to restrict this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.73,
          "end": 40.81,
          "en": "and define conditions when this code should run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.81,
          "end": 44.11,
          "en": "So that it does not always run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.11,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "For this we call useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 48.96,
          "en": "we execute this useEffect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.96,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "directly in our component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 56.47,
          "en": "and then useEffect once two arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.47,
          "end": 59.27,
          "en": "The first argument is a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.27,
          "end": 63.41,
          "en": "And here I will pass in an anonymous arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.41,
          "end": 66.44,
          "en": "The second argument is an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.44,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "and array of dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 71.853,
          "en": "And I'll come back to this array in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.75,
          "end": 76.61,
          "en": "Now, inside of this first argument inside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.61,
          "end": 79.83,
          "en": "we can execute our batch code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 84.293,
          "en": "So cut this and add this into this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 88.19,
          "en": "Now this effect function is first argument here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.19,
          "end": 90.143,
          "en": "which we passed to useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.143,
          "end": 94.34,
          "en": "will be executed by React on our behalf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.34,
          "end": 97.07,
          "en": "But only under certain circumstances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.07,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "not always when this component re-runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 104.03999999999999,
          "en": "I'll come back to those circumstances in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 107.9,
          "en": "Now with that, we make sure that our fetch request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.9,
          "end": 110.95,
          "en": "our fetch function is only executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.95,
          "end": 114.44,
          "en": "when React executes this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.44,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now when does React execute this function though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "If we would not specify this second argument this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 124.61,
          "en": "If we would omit this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.61,
          "end": 127.48,
          "en": "then this effect function would execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.48,
          "end": 130.93,
          "en": "whenever this component function executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.93,
          "end": 133.9,
          "en": "So then we don't gain anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.9,
          "end": 136.94,
          "en": "That's why you need this second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.94,
          "end": 138.38,
          "en": "You technically don't need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.38,
          "end": 140.53,
          "en": "It's not required, but if you omit it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.53,
          "end": 144.23,
          "en": "there is no difference compared to just running the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.23,
          "end": 145.53,
          "en": "in the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "With this second argument added though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 150.98,
          "en": "React will check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.98,
          "end": 152.85,
          "en": "the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 154.7,
          "en": "you add, to this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.7,
          "end": 158.69,
          "en": "and compare them to their equivalents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.69,
          "end": 162.95,
          "en": "when this effect function was executed the last time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.95,
          "end": 166.82,
          "en": "Now, if that's an empty array, there are no dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.82,
          "end": 170.66,
          "en": "And then React will only execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.66,
          "end": 173.81,
          "en": "when this component function rendered and executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.81,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "And for subsequent executions of this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "this effect function will not run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.16,
          "end": 184.46,
          "en": "because we have no dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.46,
          "end": 188.78,
          "en": "so the values of the dependencies are always the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.78,
          "end": 191.083,
          "en": "because there are no values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.4,
          "end": 196.53,
          "en": "Now, if you would add a dependency here, like let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "the Isloading state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 201.04,
          "en": "which you should not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.04,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "But if we would have this as a dependency here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 208.433,
          "en": "then this function would execute whenever the value of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.433,
          "end": 210.61,
          "en": "Isloading changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.61,
          "end": 212.66,
          "en": "So if that value does not change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.66,
          "end": 215.06,
          "en": "if that always stays the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.06,
          "end": 217.99,
          "en": "then this would also not execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.99,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "But if Isloading was false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 224.57,
          "en": "and then you somewhere update it's state to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.57,
          "end": 227.84,
          "en": "then the value of Isloading would have changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.84,
          "end": 231.023,
          "en": "and then this effect function would execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.21,
          "end": 234.75,
          "en": "Now, in reality, you don't need to think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.75,
          "end": 238.52,
          "en": "which values should trigger your effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.52,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "instead there is a simple rule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 242.9,
          "en": "In your dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.9,
          "end": 246.4,
          "en": "you should add all external values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.4,
          "end": 249.55,
          "en": "your effect function relies on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.55,
          "end": 253.26,
          "en": "So in this case, there are no external values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 256.26,
          "en": "The fetch function is a built in browser function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.26,
          "end": 259.89,
          "en": "it's not one of our component props or state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.89,
          "end": 264.34,
          "en": "And other than that we don't use any state or prop values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.34,
          "end": 268.21,
          "en": "in this effect function that would belong to our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.21,
          "end": 271.68,
          "en": "If we would extract some data from props here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.68,
          "end": 274.05,
          "en": "if we would, for example, get the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.9,
          "end": 277.15999999999997,
          "en": "from props.url let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.15999999999997,
          "end": 279.8,
          "en": "then props would be a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.8,
          "end": 282.51,
          "en": "and we should add props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.51,
          "end": 283.83,
          "en": "But that's not the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.83,
          "end": 286.25,
          "en": "but that is how it would (indistinct) then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.25,
          "end": 288.8,
          "en": "Set Isoading and set loaded meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.8,
          "end": 292.4,
          "en": "actually technically would be external dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 292.4,
          "end": 295.82,
          "en": "because these are constants defined outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.82,
          "end": 297.52,
          "en": "of this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.52,
          "end": 301.71,
          "en": "But these state updating functions are an exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.71,
          "end": 305.96,
          "en": "You can add them here and that would not be incorrect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.96,
          "end": 309.38,
          "en": "that these functions are external dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.38,
          "end": 311.72,
          "en": "And whenever these functions change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.72,
          "end": 313.73,
          "en": "this effect should run again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.73,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "because then these functions might do different things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 319.9,
          "en": "than they did the last time they were executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.9,
          "end": 322.88,
          "en": "but React actually guarantees that these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.88,
          "end": 326.42,
          "en": "state updating functions will never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.42,
          "end": 329.72,
          "en": "They will always do exactly the same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 329.72,
          "end": 334.19,
          "en": "And therefore it's allowed to omit these functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.19,
          "end": 338.73,
          "en": "And hence in our scenario here, we use useEffect like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.73,
          "end": 340.97,
          "en": "With an empty dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.97,
          "end": 344.17,
          "en": "since we have no external dependencies here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 344.17,
          "end": 347.84000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore this code will only run once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 347.84000000000003,
          "end": 351.653,
          "en": "when this component is rendered for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.88,
          "end": 357.36,
          "en": "Now I dive way deeper into useEffect with more examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 357.36,
          "end": 362.36,
          "en": "and also more features of this hook in my course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.38,
          "end": 366.7,
          "en": "But what you learn here, is the core foundation of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 366.7,
          "end": 368.93,
          "en": "which you have to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.93,
          "end": 372.49,
          "en": "that you can use it for running such side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.49,
          "end": 373.9,
          "en": "as they are called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.9,
          "end": 376.35,
          "en": "Code which does not directly influence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.35,
          "end": 378.24,
          "en": "what's showing up on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.24,
          "end": 380.04,
          "en": "And that for such side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.04,
          "end": 382.79,
          "en": "useEffect is the proper solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.79,
          "end": 386.283,
          "en": "for controlling when this code should run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 387.79,
          "end": 390.95,
          "en": "Now with that, we actually should also set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 390.95,
          "end": 392.90999999999997,
          "en": "Isloading to true here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.90999999999997,
          "end": 395.56,
          "en": "at the beginning of this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.56,
          "end": 398.3,
          "en": "so that whenever this affect would run again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.3,
          "end": 400.29,
          "en": "we set this to true again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.29,
          "end": 403.3,
          "en": "It does run again here, but still that is cleaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 403.3,
          "end": 404.81,
          "en": "I would argue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.81,
          "end": 407.53,
          "en": "And then we sent this request and ultimately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 407.53,
          "end": 409.89,
          "en": "we update our loading state again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 409.89,
          "end": 414.6,
          "en": "and we set our loaded meetups to the data we fetched here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 414.6,
          "end": 417.64,
          "en": "And now with that, its still won't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 417.64,
          "end": 420.13,
          "en": "because setting the data like this is incorrect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 420.13,
          "end": 421.51,
          "en": "as it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 421.51,
          "end": 424.35,
          "en": "but we don't have an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 424.35,
          "end": 428.06,
          "en": "And I hope I could make it clear why that's the case.",
